cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  The project keeps history, not versions: cite the commit you read, by its hash and date, and the repository
  URL. There are no releases or tags by rule (AGENTS.md, section VI).
title: "Stochology: Judgement and Decision under Uncertainty"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Neto
    given-names: Silvano
    email: dev@silvanoneto.com
repository-code: https://github.com/0b3st4f3r4/estocologia
url: https://obestafera.com
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A working text and an apparatus in Rust on judgement and decision under uncertainty: 21 chapters with
  fixed-seed laboratories, instruments over ten public datasets, seven gates able to fail a claim, and a
  public record of the errors found in the text and the code, with both values.
keywords:
  - decision under uncertainty
  - calibration
  - causal invariance
  - non-ergodicity
  - reproducibility
